<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - Australian merchandise imports rose in August.</title>
<headline>RTRS - Australian merchandise imports rose in August.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian merchandise imports rose one percent in August to A$6.215 billion seasonally adjusted from A$6.145 billion in July, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>This compares with seasonally adjusted imports of A$6.316 billion in August 1995.</p>
<p>In unadjusted terms, merchandise imports fell six percent to A$6.566 billion in August from A$6.953 billion in July and compared to A$6.953 billion also in August 1995.</p>
<p>Economists' median forecast had been for a 2.2 percent rise in seasonally adjusted imports in August.  </p>
<p>    SEASONALLY ADJ	August 96     July 96   August 95</p>
<p>    Merchandise imports  6.215 bln   6.145 bln   6.316 bln</p>
<p>    Consumption goods    1.813 bln   1.680 bln   1.690 bln</p>
<p>    Capital goods	  1.445 bln   1.386 bln   1.495 bln</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods   2.957 bln   3.079 bln   3.131 bln</p>
<p>UNADJUSTED</p>
<p>    Merchandise imports  6.566 bln   6.953 bln   6.953 bln</p>
<p>    Consumption goods    1.910 bln   1.937 bln   1.875 bln</p>
<p>    Capital goods	  1.556 bln   1.569 bln   1.670 bln</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods   3.100 bln   3.447 bln   3.408 bln</p>
<p>The bureau said seasonally adjusted imports of consumption goods rose eight percent in August, capital goods rose four percent and intermediate goods fell four percent.</p>
<p>The bureau said that in original terms, imports of civil aircraft rose A$109 million, which included the import of a Qantas aircraft valued at A$96 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
